  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target audience is individuals who are familiar with or find humor in racially charged, historically coded stereotypes, particularly those who may be exposed to or normalize anti-Black racist tropes such as comparing Black people to 'black tires' and 'color TV'. The meme is designed to provoke laughter at the expense of Black people, so the intended audience likely includes people who are either unaware of the harmful nature of these stereotypes or who find them amusing, thereby reinforcing harmful racial biases. The use of a child as a visual punchline may also target audiences who find innocence or childlike expressions amusing, even when paired with offensive content.",
